                          "fill": "$ink",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "The step counter double-counts when a patient shuffles. Most false steps in the March recordings come from heel lift under 18 N, which reads as a new strike.\n\nSee [[Sensor sampling rates]] for why 100 Hz misses the short lifts, and [[Clinic recording protocol]] for how the sessions were taken.\n\n## Next\n- [x] Mark the 41 false steps by hand in session 3\n- [ ] Raise the heel strike threshold to 18 N and rerun sessions 1–6\n- [ ] Log raw pressure at 200 Hz for one walk\n- [ ] Ask the clinic for two shuffling recordings\n- [ ] Compare the false steps with [[se",
                          "lineHeight": 1.7,
                          "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                          "fontSize": 15,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
